    "body": "I'd call it a workaround.\n\nBikeshed's behavior is that if you have:\n\n``` html\n<pre class=\"link-defaults\">\nspec: html; type: dfn; text: origin; for: /\n</pre>\n```\n\nit'll look for definitions of `origin` with no `for` value in HTML whether or not they are marked for export. That's helpful in that it lets us work around missing `export` markers in specs, but it's counter-productive when we're actually just trying to set a default `for` value. @tabatkins said he'll find some way to distinguish the two, at which point this annotation can probably go away.\n",
    "created_at": "2016-08-22T21:38:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-22T21:38:19Z",
